# Providers and Automation

## Providers

All hypervisor ops go through `lib/providers/base.py`.

- `libvirt.py` - KVM/QEMU (v1)
- `hyperv.py` - Hyper-V Local Nest (PowerShell)
- Free HEAD Nest registry: **Local Nest only** (#620 / ADR-0044). Remote Nest is Enterprise Nest Agent (#345)
- Guest provision stays in `lib/provision.py` (WinRM for Windows guests)

```
❌ Add a method to BaseProvider "just in case" or for one provider only
✅ Implement in the Nest provider using existing BaseProvider methods;
   extend base.py only if every provider must support it
❌ Revive Nest SSH/WinRM transport on free HEAD - that left in #620
❌ Change provider capability without updating the support matrix
✅ When Nest/provider support changes, update `docs/providers/`
```

Docs: [`docs/providers/`](../../docs/providers/) (feature matrix + inventories), [`docs/enterprise/`](../../docs/enterprise/) (Remote Nest).

## Answer files

User-owned templates under `automation/answerfiles/` (Clutch `answer_file` + `answer_file_parameters`). Hatch render lives in `lib/answerfile.py` (frontmatter, system tokens, companions). Nest providers pack and attach media - do not hard-wire floppy into operator surfaces.

```
❌ Silent Controller shadow Jinja under templates/answerfiles/
❌ Hardcode Autounattend paths in the Flask route
✅ Call answerfile helpers; new guests = sample Answer File + validation/OS enum
```

Win11 / Server 2025 need UEFI + TPM (`swtpm`).

## Provisioning

`lib/provision.py`: WinRM for Windows; SSH later for Linux.

